From: Claude
Subject: precompute: drop GP + KNN — align precompute models with DOWNSTREAM_MODELS

By default, find_best_hybrid resolves `models=None` at speed='full' to all
tier-full models, which includes `gp` and `knn`. But every experiment reads
`best_by_model[name]` filtered against `_shared.DOWNSTREAM_MODELS`:

    DOWNSTREAM_MODELS = ['rf', 'xgboost', 'ridge', 'svm', 'mlp', 'lightgbm']

GP + KNN results are cached but never consumed. For small datasets (antibody
n=100-250) where these models aren't sample-count-guarded, this adds ~25%
to precompute wall time per job — 6× 8h on antibody = ~12h wasted per full
precompute wave.

This patch adds `--models rf,xgboost,ridge,svm,mlp,lightgbm` to every
precompute submit script. precompute_hybrids.py already supports the
`--models` CLI arg (tests/precompute_hybrids.py:423).

CACHE IMPACT: existing cache entries (8-model `model_names`) will cache-miss
against new experiment reads (6-model `model_names`). Existing cache entries
are NOT invalidated — they remain on disk with their old keys; they just
won't be hit unless an experiment explicitly passes `models=None`. Effect is
that the NEXT precompute wave after applying this patch recomputes from
scratch with 6 models, writing fresh cache entries under new keys.

Only merge this AFTER the current wave (11825801-11825990, submitted
2026-04-22) has run to completion. Merging mid-wave creates two cache-key
generations in parallel.

